comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:02:38.401Z",claude-code-agent,"Duplicate-check evidence: all-status search over scale, create, claim, RSS, memory, and benchmark terms found the closed harness pm-mi2x and the living scale epic pm-9rxu, but no open item owning this current fixed-budget regression. Filed as a focused child of pm-9rxu."
  "2026-07-24T12:40:37.906Z",codex-root-agent,"Implementation start: claimed as an actively worked part of the broad SDK workspace mutation integrity PR. TDD scope covers deterministic id allocation, atomic stale-lock takeover, init cache and merge-fence ownership, schema migration idempotency/recovery, cross-runtime machine channels, and the fixed 10k performance gate."
  "2026-07-24T13:04:03.722Z",codex-root-agent,"Evidence update: unmodified Node 26 gate remains red after application optimizations (create best 376ms and 140640256 RSS; claim 138436608 RSS). Node 22 after removing redundant pre-lock probes improved create best from 345ms to 320ms and both RSS ceilings pass, but latency remains 10ms over the fixed gate. Budgets remain untouched; item stays active pending a real startup optimization."
  "2026-07-24T13:49:03.365Z",codex-root-agent,"Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/673 (broad SDK workspace mutation and migration primitives)."
  "2026-07-24T14:28:08.698Z",codex-root-agent,"Clarification for PR #673 review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/673 is a related PR that delivered safe supporting optimizations only. This performance issue remains open and unresolved pending Node 26 create-latency and create/claim RSS recovery under the unchanged fixed budgets; no delivery/closure claim is intended."
  "2026-07-24T19:20:34.794Z",claude-code-agent,"Fresh unchanged-budget baseline on main-derived branch under Node 26.5.0: cli.create best 386ms > 310ms and peak RSS 138899456 > 115184640; cli.claim peak RSS 138924032 > 118031360. Disabling Node compile cache worsened latency and still used 137MB RSS, so compile-cache retention is not the root cause. Budgets remain unchanged."
  "2026-07-24T20:08:24.767Z",claude-code-agent,"Evidence: unchanged pnpm benchmark:scale:check passed three consecutive runs under supported Node v22.21.1. cli.create min was 275ms, 286ms, and 287ms (budget 310ms); create peak RSS was 102768640, 104648704, and 102649856 bytes (budget 115184640); claim peak RSS was 102375424, 103870464, and 104419328 bytes (budget 118031360). SDK create remained 5-7ms. Budgets, iteration count, transports, and feature coverage were unchanged. Root cause was startup parse cost compounded by default full-corpus similarity work; fixed via opt-in default governance, dependency-light scoring, selective create registration, cached settings reuse, and production bundle minification with source maps."
  "2026-07-24T22:21:49.401Z",claude-code-agent,"Release evidence: the complete release suite passed build, typecheck, docs/skills, static quality, exact 100% coverage (43045 statements, 30524 branches, 8760 functions, 41831 lines; 6249 tests), version policy, secret scan, packed npx, compatibility, package-first dogfood, and Sentry/telemetry. Greptile correctly deferred because the branch was not committed yet and will run on the PR. Clean installed-package and ten-package external smoke proofs also passed."
  "2026-07-24T22:26:06.420Z",claude-code-agent,"Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/684"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:06:04.040Z",claude-code-agent,"Reproduction environment: current main at d96dfc85, pm 2026.7.24-3, Node v26.5.0, pnpm 11.10.0. The gate failure is evidence of budget drift, not permission to change scripts/bench/scale-budgets.json. Reproduce across supported Node versions before attributing the regression solely to application code."
