close_reason: "Fixed the unchanged Node 22 scale budgets through minified production bundling, selective mutation registration, cached settings reuse, dependency-light scoring, and zero-overhead default duplicate governance; three consecutive gate runs and the full release suite passed."
body: "Current-main evidence: benchmark:scale:check ran the checked-in 10k fixture and preserved the fixed budget manifest. CLI create best/min was 363 ms against 310 ms; create peak RSS was 139,964,416 bytes against 115,184,640; claim peak RSS was 138,199,040 against 118,031,360. Read-path p95 remained below one second and all default outputs stayed below 5k estimated tokens. The implementation must diagnose allocation/startup causes and restore the existing budgets without raising thresholds, excluding paths, weakening iterations, or removing behavior. SDK parity and tiny-project responsiveness are guardrails."
